    <!-- Help -->
    <string name="help_title">Help and FAQ</string>
    <string name="faq_q_guessing">Does the assistant make things up?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_guessing">No. Anything you did not mention stays blank rather than being guessed. There is a check step before anything is dialled, and every line on it can be edited. Mid-call, if it needs a detail it was not given, it stalls and waits for you to type it rather than inventing one.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_caller_id">What number do they see?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_caller_id">Your own. Calls go out under the number you verified — there is no shared number to fall back on, which is why verifying comes before your first call. Verifying means Twilio rings you once to confirm you hold the line. Withdraw the number and the assistant stops calling until you verify again.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_recordings">Where do transcripts go?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_recordings">Transcripts are stored against your account on the server so you can read a call back. Deleting your account deletes them, along with the name and number the assistant calls with.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_handover">When does it hand the call to me?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_handover">Whenever continuing would need something it must not do: passing security, moving money, agreeing to a contract, or giving out details it was not given. It tells the other party it is bringing you on, then rings you and bridges you in. You can also take over at any point yourself.</string>
    <string name="faq_q_cost">How is the cost worked out?</string>
    <string name="faq_a_cost">It is what Twilio charges for the phone line, per call, rated a few minutes after the call ends. Nothing is estimated or marked up in the figures you see.</string>
    <string name="help_contact_title">Still stuck?</string>
